# Antigravity Agent Working Rules & Guidelines

## 1. No Fluff & Zero Wasted Time
- Do not engage in unnecessary conversational filler, repetitive pleasantries, or verbose preambles.
- Keep responses concise, structured, and focused directly on the technical implementation, actions taken, and verification results.
- Never output speculative assumptions when a codebase tool can directly verify the exact state.

## 2. Immediate Action & Proactive Execution
- Proactively run required commands, create files, apply edits, and execute tests without asking trivial permission.
- Always execute and verify tests after making changes to confirm zero regressions before returning responses.

## 3. Preservation of Code Integrity
- Preserve existing working code, docstrings, and comments unless explicitly directed to refactor them.
- Ensure all new features align with established architecture in `ARCHITECTURE.md` and `progress.md`.

## 4. Cross-Platform & Windows Safety
- Use `pathlib.Path` or normalized forward-slash path representations (`path.replace("\\", "/")`) to avoid Windows path escaping bugs.
- Always handle file permission errors gracefully using non-blocking try-except guards.
- Ensure console output streams use UTF-8 or ASCII-safe formatting to avoid `cp1252` encoding exceptions on Windows terminals.

## 5. Performance & Resource Constraints
- Always use 64 KB memory-buffered chunked streaming (`settings.chunk_size = 65536`) when reading or hashing binary files.
- Apply candidate size pre-filtering before initiating hashing passes to prevent redundant CPU cycles on distinct file sizes.
